 "description": "The Blue Line Voice — Blood, Sand & Smoke.\nBlood for the officers who bleed on the streets. Sand for the veterans who bled in the desert. Smoke for every burn pit, every structure fire, every toxic exposure the system refuses to own.\nFor veterans, law enforcement, firefighters, paramedics, EMTs, nurses, and dispatchers — the ones who run toward it and spend the rest of their lives dealing with what that cost them.\nJ. Weddell — Air Force veteran, burn pit survivor, former officer, author of Still Breathing. He operated heavy equipment inside the burn pit at Ali Air Base, Iraq. He came home, put on a badge, and worked the streets of upstate New York. He spent twenty years fighting to be believed. Now he's talking.\nBurn pits. Toxic exposure. Line-of-duty injuries. Broken systems. Real stories. No filter.\nIf you served. If you responded. If you're still in the fight — this is your channel.\nSubscribe. Share. Make noise.\n",
